# Cursor Rules for AI Manager (9router-gateway)

## Project Overview
AI Manager is a high-performance Go reverse proxy, authentication gateway, and admin dashboard positioned in front of 9router Core (127.0.0.1:20128).

## Go Standards
- Target Go 1.22+ conventions.
- Always run `go fmt ./...` and `go vet ./...` clean.
- Use `zerolog` (`github.com/rs/zerolog/log`) for structured logging. Avoid `log.Println` or bare `fmt.Println` in production code.
- Always wrap errors with `%w`: `fmt.Errorf("action failed: %w", err)`.
- Always pass `r.Context()` to repository methods, database queries, and outbound HTTP requests.

## SQLite & Repository
- SQLite driver is `modernc.org/sqlite` (pure Go).
- Always use WAL mode and busy timeout pragma:
  `_pragma=busy_timeout(5000)&_pragma=journal_mode(WAL)&_pragma=foreign_keys(1)`.
- ALWAYS use parameterized queries with `?`. Never format user input directly into SQL strings.
- Add new schema changes to `migrate()` in `internal/database/db.go`.

## Reverse Proxy & SSE Streaming
- Do not set a write timeout on `http.Server` (must be `WriteTimeout: 0`) to avoid terminating long-running SSE LLM completions.
- In SSE streaming proxy logic, flush chunks immediately via `http.Flusher`.
- Intercept token usage from SSE stream lines (`data: {"usage": ...}`) or calculate heuristic token approximations on completion.
- Exact match cache uses SHA-256 hash of model + messages + temperature with 15m TTL.

## Auth & Security
- Never expose port 20128 (9router Core) to the public network; only bind to 127.0.0.1.
- API keys must be generated using `handlers.GenerateSecureAPIKey("sk-gw-...")`.
- Password hashes use `bcrypt` with cost 12.
- Session tokens are 64-character random hex strings stored server-side in the SQLite `sessions` table.
- Enforce role boundaries: `admin` vs `user`.

## Templates & Web UI
- HTML templates live in `web/templates/` and inherit from `base.html`.
- Render with `h.render(w, r, "page.html", "base.html", data)`.
- Static files live in `web/static/` and are embedded via `embed.FS` in `web/web.go`.
